# openSUSE keeps the extra Plasma packages in their own OBS repository, so it
# has to exist before `kde-packages` can resolve. Debian needs no equivalent,
# which is why there is no `run.debian` and the unit reports a platform skip
# there rather than pretending to do something.
#
# `zypper ar` refuses a URI it already has, under any alias, so re-adding is a
# failure rather than a no-op. The probe is what makes this unit safe to force
# on its own — without it, forcing this without also forcing `repos` (which
# clears every repository first) would fail on the duplicate.
kind: action
capabilities: kde
requires: repos
root: yes
unless: zypper lr 2>/dev/null | grep -qi 'kde:extra'
